<p local-id=3D"62d1e77bffa8"><code>[Insert Retrospective Opinion from =C3=
=81milie]</code></p>
<h3 local-id=3D"03e9e970b04a" id=3D"RetrospectiveBoard-Ralph.1"><code>Ralph=
</code></h3>
<p local-id=3D"580acde01517"><code>[Insert Retrospective Opinion from Ralph=
]</code></p>
<p local-id=3D"b6d525afcc05"></p>
<h1 local-id=3D"6515b331f148" id=3D"RetrospectiveBoard-Sprint1-Concepting&a=
mp;Research">Sprint 1 - Concepting &amp; Research</h1>
<h2 local-id=3D"336d93ddfbf9" id=3D"RetrospectiveBoard-GroupFeedback.1">Gro=
up Feedback</h2>
<p local-id=3D"bfc2d19e7267"><code>The first sprint has been a slow affair.=
 Whilst we were able to get most of our objectives complete. However a sign=
ificant amount of the work was completed by only two individuals, with the =
other two being mostly absent-- Additionally Communication has been lack lu=
ster, not only between group members but also between the stakeholders. </c=
ode></p>
<p local-id=3D"5895a3ab32a7">In future sprints we must aim towards establis=
hing weekly correspondence with both the client and stakeholder. Whilst it =
is too early to be enforcing anything, we must hold each other more account=
able and push for more communication between members about attendance and w=
ork done. Especially with us being out of the concepting phase, it is param=
ount that coding work gets complete and tests get rolled out.</p>
<h2 local-id=3D"d026be6f5d11" id=3D"RetrospectiveBoard-IndividualisedFeedba=
ck.1">Individualised Feedback</h2>
<h3 local-id=3D"68001b6ea4fb" id=3D"RetrospectiveBoard-Luc.2"><code>Luc</co=
de></h3>
<p local-id=3D"6782e7b6c7b9"><code>Luc was generally the best performing me=
mber of this sprint, having been the most communicative between group membe=
rs and been the one with the best attendance rate. This sprint he put signi=
ficant effort in critiquing the concept and then realising it through a vis=
ualised process chart. Additional efforts of his has shone through in keepi=
ng group cohesion, setting up the GitHub and trying to keep not only himsel=
f but also others accountable. </code><br><br>
However there has been some issues, namely with client communication and de=
reliction of his duties in being the bridge between the group and the clien=
t following the initial meet up.</p>
<h3 local-id=3D"e441750c3541" id=3D"RetrospectiveBoard-=C3=81milie.2"><code=
>=C3=81milie</code></h3>
<p local-id=3D"53daefe4214a"><code>[Insert Feedback on =C3=81milie]</code><=
/p>
<h3 local-id=3D"d51c639ab311" id=3D"RetrospectiveBoard-Ralph.2"><code>Ralph=
</code></h3>
<p local-id=3D"ca139a7c32a5"><code>Ralph's work this sprint generally consi=
sted of a singular wire frame created without research or documentation. Hi=
s performance this sprint has been poor in terms of contribution to discuss=
ion, communication, attendance, workload and initiative. </code><br><br>
He has alot to work on, namely in seeking his passion and energy in the pro=
ject, as it feels like he is demotivated and unwilling to put in more than =
the bare minimum of energy. He has indicated that he is pushing to improve,=
 however only time can tell whether this will be the case.</p>
<p local-id=3D"9163d187c54f">Yoeri</p>
<p local-id=3D"56b1cd8a747c">Generally well performing when at campus, howe=
ver he has been rarely at campus. His main contribution was assisting with =
a research initiative however not much else outside of that. Other than his=
 attendance, his communication has also been poor but has improved over tim=
e.</p>
<p local-id=3D"e18b0eb911f6">Generally he needs to work on his attendance s=
o that he is actually present for when work needs to be done. In addition t=
o communicating better with the other group individuals with regards to wor=
k load and attendance.</p>
<h2 local-id=3D"de3316816eb1" id=3D"RetrospectiveBoard-IndividualOpinions.1=
">Individual Opinions</h2>
<h3 local-id=3D"e0ce699ede70" id=3D"RetrospectiveBoard-Luc.3"><code>Luc</co=
de></h3>
<p local-id=3D"19c87e4f7de0"><code>Personal: I feel like I did decent work =
when I was here. I wrote a research document and I worked on getting the pr=
oject on the rails with the group, or with whoever happened to be there tha=
t day. Besides monday-thursday I did very little though. A lot of days I ha=
d work and even if I didn't I would fill the time with cycling or doomscrol=
ling or going to a movie over getting work done. I'm not really happy with =
how productive I was, I basically only made one document and that's it. I d=
idn't get in contact with the stakeholder, and I'm overall a bit of a disas=
ter in terms of the digital communication in the group. Not having standups=
 also means I don't have the moment on the day to get started compared to w=
hat I maybe should have. Overall would give this sprint a 4/10 on my end.</=
code></p>
<p local-id=3D"9c0ddc0f3aa8"></p>
<p local-id=3D"ca0819de4b35"><code>Group: I think if we'd kept attendance f=
or just the mondays and thursdays we'd be at less than 50%. I was late a fe=
w days but some people had commitments, and sickness plagued the group too.=
 Some people are very lax about it which I don't like. Communication was ba=
d. We do not have a formal standup schedule, and I have no clue what story =
anyone is working on exactly because nobody is assigned to anything (includ=
ing me). We have stories but I think pushing them all to GitHub was maybe a=
 mistake in their current form? Though I have not asked, and nobody has com=
plained either. I think this is the crux of the problem, everybody works al=
ongside one another without any structured communication. I'm also not real=
ly sure if anyone is even doing anything. Even though the project is not of=
f the rails I'm not super happy about how things are going at the moment.</=
code></p>
<h3 local-id=3D"00dbf13af015" id=3D"RetrospectiveBoard-=C3=81milie.3"><code=
>=C3=81milie</code></h3>
<p local-id=3D"3aabf167bb8f"><code>Generally my performance has been okay a=
t best. I've taken alot of initaive with regards to concepting and pushing =
the group forwards and been the instigator in several manners. However I've=
 under taken issues with my own punctuality, as I have been on time only on=
ce the entire time as well as missing two days, the first wasn't communicat=
ed but the second was. I've also taken on responsibilites that I haven't fu=
lfilled, such as finishing off some of the research papers. As well as negl=
ecting to do any work outside of University hours, something which has slow=
ed down general progress. </code></p>
<p local-id=3D"89c926e1525f"><br>
During the next sprint I need to either work on my punctuality or come to a=
 new agreement within which I can better make it to the school on time. I a=
lso need to focus on getting more work done at home and outside of universi=
ty times, otherwise I will have to force myself to come in person to the Ca=
mpus.</p>
<h3 local-id=3D"14723e958f78" id=3D"RetrospectiveBoard-Ralph.3"><code>Ralph=
</code></h3>
<p local-id=3D"5c333bd80ff5"><code>During this first sprint, things went pr=
etty well overall. I was still getting used to the new group project, but m=
y teammates really helped by making the planning and task division clear an=
d manageable. This made it easier for me to understand what was expected fr=
om me and where I could contribute the most.</code></p>
<p local-id=3D"90ebb0871450"><code>In terms of attendance, I mainly showed =
up on Thursdays. For the next sprint, I want to improve this by being more =
present on Mondays as well, so I can be more involved from the start of the=
 week and stay better aligned with the team.</code></p>
<p local-id=3D"6b52cd676da5"><code>My main responsibility this sprint was w=
orking on the wireframes. I was also assigned the Web App UI, which means I=
 am focusing on the visual side of the project. This allowed me to think ab=
out layout, user flow, and how the design supports the overall concept.</co=
de></p>
<p local-id=3D"f829c2bf1d2e"><code>For the next sprint, I want to focus mor=
e on developing a clear research question to support our design decisions. =
I also plan to improve the visuals further and start implementing the wiref=
rames into an actual dashboard. In addition, I want to present and explain =
the wireframes to the stakeholders, so we can gather feedback early and mak=
e sure we are moving in the right direction.</code></p>
    </div>
